afk: add task.isolation.autoApply (default true).

Motivation: upstream always merges an isolated task's captured changes
back into the parent worktree the moment the subagent finishes. With
many parallel isolated subagents that races concurrent edits and dirties
the orchestrator's worktree mid-flight. autoApply=false (set in
nix/afk.nix config.yml) keeps each task's changes parked on its
refs/omp/task/<id> ref and only announces where they live, so the
orchestrator cherry-picks against a clean tree (mirrors eval
agent(apply=false)).

What must survive a rebase:
- The setting (settings-schema) and the executor short-circuit: when
  isolated && !autoApply, skip mergeIsolatedChanges, keep the ref/patch,
  and append the "changes captured on branch `omp/task/<id>` ... Not
  merged." notice to the task result text — the distribution's merge
  rule tells agents to read the ref name from that notice.
- eval agent()'s explicit apply= argument still overrides per call.

